    {
      "layer": "economic_commercial",
      "tag": "champagne_fair_hub",
      "direction": "rise",
      "description": "The six annual Champagne Fairs, held at Troyes, Provins, Lagny, and Bar-sur-Aube, were the primary nexus of European long-distance commerce from the 12th to 14th centuries. Italian merchants met Flemish cloth merchants here under safe-conduct that made Champagne a trading zone with international legal standing.",
